# Everything the tools write for one machine mid-flight lives under
# .vstack/local/, one directory per tool: frozen wireframe versions, annotations
# and threads; the JSON bridge's seq counters, version history, and `url` files
# naming a live localhost port. None of it belongs in the repo. The rest of
# .vstack/ — pipeline.json, specs/, build/ — is the pipeline and does, so this
# ignores local/ rather than the whole thing. It sits beside the artifact it
# belongs to, hence the leading **/.
**/.vstack/local/

# Recording the README demo installs playwright-core at the repo root.
node_modules/

# A host writes this into the plugin directory when it installs from this clone
# as a local marketplace, which is how the plugin is tested before it ships. It
# is that machine's install bookkeeping, not part of the plugin.
plugins/vstack/.orphaned_at

.DS_Store
.env
